# TradingView Refined Supertrend ATR TSL

## Source
- Source: [[sources/tradingview-mechanical-strategy-scripts]]
- Page / Timestamp: TradingView script `Refined Supertrend ATR + TSL + Filters [Nifty/BankNifty] V2`, author handle `vimalboiling`, open-source strategy, accessed 2026-05-22, page shows May 7, https://www.tradingview.com/script/c1XpwWU4-Refined-Supertrend-ATR-TSL-Filters-Nifty-BankNifty-V2/

## Mechanics

### Entry
Use M15 baseline.

- Long setup:
  - Price crosses above SuperTrend line.
  - If EMA filter enabled, price closes above EMA(200).
  - If ADX filter enabled, ADX(14) > 20.
  - Session filter optional.
- Short setup:
  - Price crosses below SuperTrend line.
  - If EMA filter enabled, price closes below EMA(200).
  - If ADX filter enabled, ADX(14) > 20.
  - Session filter optional.

### Exit
V5 baseline converts source partial exits into one position with one managed stop:

- Initial target checkpoint: when price reaches +1.5 * ATR(14), move stop to breakeven.
- Runner exit: trail stop at the more conservative of SuperTrend line and custom ATR trail.
- Optional fixed target axis: exit all at 3.0 * ATR(14) if no trailing improvement.

### Stop Loss
- Long stop: max(SuperTrend line, close - 2.0 * ATR(14)) once in trade.
- Short stop: min(SuperTrend line, close + 2.0 * ATR(14)) once in trade.
- Before trail activation, use the SuperTrend line as the primary stop.

### Position Sizing
V5 default: fixed-risk $1,000 for P2 baseline, one position per symbol/magic.

### Zusatzliche Filter
- Source default SuperTrend ATR length 10, factor 3.0.
- Source default EMA filter enabled and ADX filter enabled.
- Source market Nifty/BankNifty is ported to DWX index CFDs.

## Concepts (what kind of strategy is this)
- [[concepts/trend-following]] - enters on SuperTrend state change.
- [[concepts/volatility-stop]] - ATR and SuperTrend define exits.
- [[concepts/trend-filter]] - EMA(200) and ADX filter choppy/counter-trend trades.

